# Phaser Collision Optimization Techniques

## Context
- When implementing physics systems in Phaser games with many interactive entities
- When experiencing framerate drops during collision-heavy scenarios in Phaser
- When implementing custom collision shapes or detection mechanics
- When building games that require efficient collision handling on mobile devices

## Requirements
- Use Phaser 3.70+ collision groups and collision categories for efficient filtering
- Implement proper active/inactive state management for physics bodies
- Use Phaser's direct control mode for performance-critical objects
- Configure appropriate physics body types (static, dynamic, fixed) based on object behavior
- Leverage Phaser's spatial partitioning for efficient collision detection
- Disable collision for off-screen objects using Phaser's camera bounds
- Profile collision performance using Phaser's built-in debugging tools

