## Phaser 3.70+ Collision Optimization Techniques

### 1. Use Collision Groups for Efficient Filtering

```typescript
// Define collision groups
const GROUPS = {
  PLAYER: 1,
  ENEMY: 2,
  PROJECTILE: 3,
  OBSTACLE: 4
};

// Configure player physics body
const playerBody = player.body;
playerBody.setCollisionGroup(GROUPS.PLAYER);

// Set what groups the player can collide with
playerBody.setCollidesWith([GROUPS.ENEMY, GROUPS.OBSTACLE]);

// Example: Make projectiles only hit enemies
projectileBody.setCollisionGroup(GROUPS.PROJECTILE);
projectileBody.setCollidesWith([GROUPS.ENEMY]);
```

### 2. Enable Direct Control for Performance

```typescript
// Enable direct control mode for performance-critical objects
// Available in Phaser 3.70+
playerBody.setDirectControl(true);

// Direct control bypasses some physics calculations for better performance
// Best used for player characters or objects under direct input control
```

### 3. Use Efficient Physics Body Types

```typescript
// Static bodies for immovable objects (best performance)
const platform = scene.physics.add.staticBody(x, y, width, height);

// Dynamic bodies for objects that move and respond to forces
const movingObject = scene.physics.add.body(x, y, width, height);

// Fixed rotation bodies for better performance when rotation isn't needed
bodyA.setFixedRotation();
```

### 4. Optimize with Process Callbacks

```typescript
// Add a process callback to filter collision checks
scene.physics.add.collider(
  groupA, 
  groupB, 
  handleCollision,   // Called when collision occurs
  filterCollision,   // Called BEFORE detailed collision check
  this
);

// Efficient process function with early exit
function filterCollision(objA, objB) {
  // Skip inactive objects
  if (!objA.active || !objB.active) return false;
  
  // Skip if too far apart (broad phase)
  const dx = objA.x - objB.x;
  const dy = objA.y - objB.y;
  return (dx * dx + dy * dy) < 10000; // 100 pixel radius squared
}
```

### 5. Efficiently Manage Active Bodies

```typescript
// Disable physics for off-screen objects
function optimizeOffscreenObjects(group, camera) {
  const visibleBounds = camera.getBounds();
  // Add padding to prevent pop-in
  visibleBounds.inflate(200, 200);
  
  group.getChildren().forEach(obj => {
    const body = obj.body;
    const visible = visibleBounds.contains(body.x, body.y);
    
    // Enable/disable based on visibility
    body.enable = visible;
  });
}
```

### 6. Use Phaser's World Bounds Efficiently

```typescript
// Configure world bounds for better performance
scene.physics.world.setBounds(0, 0, map.widthInPixels, map.heightInPixels);

// Enable bounds collision only where needed
scene.physics.world.setBoundsCollision(true, true, true, true);

// For large worlds, only update physics near the camera
scene.physics.world.step(regionX, regionY, regionWidth, regionHeight);
```

